UPDATE companies SET description='The Great Plains Energy Corridor was established in 2008 at Bismarck State College in Bismarck, North Dakota, through the initiative of former U.S. Senator Byron Dorgan.

It leverages Bismarck State College''s nationally recognized energy education programs, which deliver state-of-the-art training to current and future industry employees. The Corridor''s office is housed in the National Energy Center of Excellence (NECE) building on the BSC campus, a facility dedicated in September 2008 that incorporates a ground-source geothermal heat pump system, LEED-compliant lighting, a total energy heat recovery system, and Flexcrete—a construction material made with fly ash from coal combustion.

The Corridor serves partners across government, education, and the private sector, facilitating collaboration to promote energy-related activities through federal funding and other sources. The annual EmPowerND Energy Conference and the North Dakota Energy Report are among its key outreach vehicles, though the 2023 conference was canceled.

The Corridor''s distinguishing feature is its integration within a college that operates a LEED-certified, energy-efficient facility purpose-built for energy education, giving it direct access to training infrastructure and a mandate to connect diverse energy stakeholders across the state.', certifications=ARRAY['LEED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Energy education program support", "Outreach and special event coordination", "Energy industry information dissemination", "Multi-sector partnership facilitation", "Annual energy reporting and analysis", "Conference organization (EmPowerND)"], "industries": ["Energy education", "Geothermal energy", "Renewable fuels", "Sustainable development", "Energy transmission and storage", "Government energy programs", "Private sector energy development", "Workforce training"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["NECE building: ground-source geothermal heat pump system", "NECE building: LEED-compliant lighting system", "NECE building: total energy heat recovery system", "Flexcrete construction material (fly ash based)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Division of Bismarck State College with direct access to nationally recognized energy education programs", "Housed in a LEED-certified, geothermal-powered National Energy Center of Excellence building", "Facilitates cross-sector partnerships among government, education, and private industry", "Focuses on North Dakota''s full energy portfolio from geothermal to transmission storage", "Produces annual North Dakota Energy Report and EmPowerND conference"], "facts_used": ["Created at Bismarck State College in 2008 through efforts of former U.S. Senator Byron Dorgan -> /about", "Division of Bismarck State College -> /about, /", "Office located in National Energy Center of Excellence (NECE) building on BSC campus -> /about", "NECE building dedicated September 2008 -> /about", "Building has geothermal heat pump, LEED lighting, energy heat recovery, Flexcrete (fly ash) -> /about", "Provides information, education, outreach programs, special events on energy topics -> /about", "Works with partners in government, education, private sector -> /about", "Works with BSC''s nationally recognized energy education programs -> /about", "Focus on enhanced geothermal systems, renewable fuels, sustainable development, energy transmission and storage -> /about", "Department of Energy Award DE-OE0000079 -> /, products", "LEED certification mentioned for lighting -> /about", "Copyright 2026 Great Plains Energy Corridor -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "The Great Plains Energy Corridor was created at Bismarck State College in 2008... The Corridor was tasked with providing innovative approaches that bring people together to advance the development of North Dakota''s abundant and diverse energy resources.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='great-plains-energy-corridor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Green Bay Plastics, Inc. has operated from Green Bay, Wisconsin since its incorporation in 1957. Originally part of Mosinee Paper Corporation, the company was bought out in 1989 by J. Kevin Hogan and his wife JoAnn, and remains family-owned today. Michael Hogan serves as president and general manager, with Patrick Hogan as vice president and Kathleen Hogan-Lesatz as controller and secretary-treasurer.

The company specializes in custom blow molding, producing plastic bottles, jars, handled containers, and industrial components. It designs and builds its own tooling, machinery, and auxiliary equipment in-house, and offers secondary services including labeling, painting, and custom packaging. Production runs range from a few thousand units to mass-production volumes.

Green Bay Plastics serves a diverse set of industries: food and beverage, lubricants, toy components, industrial applications, medical and healthcare packaging, dietary supplements, personal care, household products, sporting goods, and appliance parts such as fluid reservoirs for dishwashers and washing machines. Its customers are primarily wholesale distributors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Blow Molding", "Custom Labeling", "Custom Packaging", "Painting", "Tooling Design and Build", "Machinery Design and Build", "HDPE Blow Molding", "Handled Container Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Food and Beverage", "Lubricants", "Toys", "Industrial", "Medical and Healthcare", "Dietary Supplements", "Personal Care", "Household Products", "Sporting Goods", "Appliances"], "materials": ["HDPE"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Production run sizes that can range from a few thousand to mass-production capabilities", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1957", "Designs and builds its own tooling, machinery, and auxiliary equipment", "Production runs from a few thousand to mass-production volumes", "Offers custom labeling, painting, and packaging services"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1957 -> db, /about-us", "Family-owned since 1957 -> /", "Hogan family ownership details -> /about-us", "Custom blow molding of bottles, jars, handled containers, industrial components -> /", "Designs and builds own tooling and machinery -> /, /about-us", "Production runs from a few thousand to mass-production -> /", "Industries served: food, lubricants, toys, industrial, medical, dietary, personal care, household, sporting goods, appliances -> /, /about-us", "Secondary services: labeling, painting, packaging -> /", "HDPE material capability -> capabilities", "Self-sufficient manufacturing approach -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Manufacturer of Blow Molded Plastic Products", "founded_year": "1957", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='green-bay-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='In 2018 the company relocated to a larger facility in North Plainfield, New Jersey, expanding its footprint to over seven times the size of its original store.

The business stocks more than 300,000 distinct line items across multiple warehouse locations, ranging from semiconductors, relays, capacitors, and resistors to wire, cable, fuses, and audio/video cables. Beyond distribution, Green Brook Electronics operates a retail storefront, an equipment rental center, a repair shop capable of board-level and surface-mount work, a movie-prop rental division featuring vintage test equipment and computers, a technology studio offering soldering and Arduino classes, a vinyl record center, and a component-identification service.

Customers include large technology firms, industrial buyers, medical-equipment operators, film-production companies, hobbyists, and the general public. The company ships worldwide and emphasizes its ability to source obsolete and long-lead-time parts.

Green Brook Electronics distinguishes itself through its deep inventory of hard-to-find components, its repair expertise across consumer and industrial electronics, and its eclectic mix of retail, rental, and educational services that serve both professional engineers and enthusiasts.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic component distribution", "Obsolete and long-lead-time component sourcing", "Equipment rental", "Electronic repair (board level, surface mount, cable, medical equipment)", "Component identification service", "Technology training and tutoring (soldering, Arduino, etc.)", "Movie prop rental (vintage test equipment, computers)", "Vinyl record and player sales"], "industries": ["Technology", "Industrial", "Medical", "Entertainment (film production)", "Education", "Consumer electronics / hobbyist"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 300,000 line items stocked across multiple warehouses", "Expertise in sourcing obsolete and long-lead-time electronic components", "Full-service repair shop for board-level, surface-mount, and medical equipment", "Equipment rental, movie-prop rental, technology classes, and vinyl record sales", "Worldwide shipping with industrial and walk-in customer support"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 -> db", "Headquarters North Plainfield, NJ -> db", "Over 300,000 line items stocked -> /", "Multiple warehouse locations -> /", "Relocated from Green Brook to North Plainfield in 2018 -> /about-us", "New store over 7 times size of original -> /about-us", "Retail store with semiconductors, relays, capacitors, resistors, wire, cable, fuses, audio/video cables -> /", "Equipment rental center -> /", "Repair center for tube amps, medical equipment, cable, board level, surface mount -> /", "Movie prop center with vintage test equipment, computers -> /", "Technology studios offering soldering, Arduino, music lessons -> /", "Vinyl center for vinta