UPDATE companies SET description='H&H Metal Fabrication operates from St. Louis, Missouri. The company traces its roots to 1947 when the Finazzo family began manufacturing light fixtures in the same building as the H&H radio shop. It has remained family-owned for over 79 years. In 2019, ownership transitioned to Carolyn Farrell (President) and Morgan Jarrett (COO), making it a certified women-owned business (WBENC). Kevin Farrell serves as CFO.

The shop specializes in custom metal fabrication built to print, including electrical enclosures, e-houses (large-scale electrical structures), custom fabricated components, panels, supports, assemblies, and specialty metal products. They also offer enclosure modification services such as cut-outs, drilling, threading, and panel changes. Their downtown plant houses a 500-ton, 22-foot press brake, indicating heavy forming capacity. They provide full painting capabilities and consultations at any design stage. No specific headcount or annual volume figures are disclosed.

Customers include engineering teams, project managers, procurement buyers, electrical contractors, manufacturers, and designers. Concrete examples: Villa Lighting Supply Inc. (lighting projects in the US and Canada), Missouri Botanical Garden (Chihuly Blue Chandelier reinstallation attachment mechanism), and St. Louis City Hall (exterior lighting housings).

