UPDATE companies SET description='Hardware Hawaii has operated as a hardware retailer in Kailua, Hawaii, since 1954. The company maintains four locations across the islands: the original Kailua store on Oahu, a Kapolei store on Oahu, a Mapunapuna store in Honolulu, and a Koloa store on Kauai.

The business stocks a range of building materials and hardware, including engineered wood I-Joists designed to reduce floor vibration, Gallina RDC storm panels for hurricane protection, and propane refills available at the Kailua, Kapolei, and Koloa stores. It also runs a screen shop that repairs or builds custom window and door screens with a turnaround of seven days or less, and offers island-wide delivery and leak-detection services.

The company serves the residential construction and home-improvement markets, with concrete examples such as supplying I-Joists for floor systems, providing storm panels ahead of hurricane season, and fabricating screens for property repairs.

