UPDATE companies SET description='Hawaii Pacific X-Ray Corporation was founded in 1986 in Honolulu, Hawaii, as a partnership between Bill Johnson, a 30-year veteran of General Electric Medical Systems sales in the islands, and his son Chris Johnson. The pair set out to create a locally owned alternative to the entrenched x-ray sales and service providers then dominating the Hawaii and Pacific Basin markets.

