UPDATE companies SET description='Highland Harmony Farm operates from Wilsall, Montana, where it raises legumes, ancient grains, berries, vegetables, and flowers while also keeping bees for raw honey. The farm runs a stone mill to produce its own flour and sells directly at the Gallatin Valley farmers market in Bozeman during summer and the Bozeman Winter Market in the colder months.

The operation centers on regenerative agriculture, a system the owners describe as nurturing the "gut biome" of soil, plants, and people alike. Practices focus on rebuilding soil biology, which they say improves nutrient density in the crops they harvest. The farm collaborates with the Natural Resources Conservation Service on conservation planning, and its stone-milled flour is processed in a dedicated mill house that visitors can tour during scheduled farm walks.

The product line spans staple grains, seasonal produce, honey, and cut flowers, all marketed under the "Grown in Montana by Folks You Know" banner. No wholesale or industrial accounts are mentioned in the available information.

