UPDATE companies SET description='Houston Transformer Company, LTD., founded in 1969, operates from a 33,000-square-foot climate-controlled facility in Houston, Texas. The company was established as a manufacturer of custom transformers, inductors, chokes, and related magnetic devices.

The company designs and builds magnetic components ranging from sub-miniature surface-mount devices to three-phase distribution transformers weighing over 1,500 pounds. Its in-house capabilities include custom core configurations (toroidal, bobbin, layer-wound, water-cooled, transposed windings), winding with copper and aluminum conductors, and a full machine shop and sheet-metal department that produce bobbins, cases, NEMA enclosures, and sensor housings. An inventory of approximately 25,000 pounds of high-grade silicon steel supports short cycle times. The engineering staff brings over 75 years of combined design experience, and the workforce of 51–200 employees handles prototype through production volumes.

Houston Transformer serves energy exploration and drilling operations, medical and biomedical equipment, military and aerospace programs, audio and lighting/LED manufacturers, data-processing and industrial-process-control systems, and communications OEMs. Products are sold in single-piece quantities as well as to original equipment manufacturers.

The company emphasizes a “can-do” philosophy and unwavering customer focus, citing continuous improvement, cycle-time reduction, and adoption of cutting-edge technology as ongoing goals. Its reputation for dependability in extreme environments—up to 450 °F (250 °C) and 10 kV—stems from rigorous testing, traceability, and compliance with UL and other industry standards.', certifications=ARRAY['UL']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom magnetic design", "Fast prototyping", "Testing and traceability", "UL and industry standards compliance", "Custom core configurations (toroidal, bobbin, layer wound, water-cooled, transposed windings)", "Copper and aluminum winding", "CNC machining", "Sheet metal fabrication (NEMA boxes, cases, cabinets)", "Encapsulation, molding, epoxy coating, canning", "Value-added assemblies", "High-voltage insulation (up to 10 kV)", "High-temperature operation (up to 450 \u00b0F)", "Large-scale transformer manufacturing (up to 250 KVA, 1500 A)", "Surface-mount magnetic assembly", "Toroidal winding (up to 25 KVA)", "Laminated and tape-wound cut-core construction", "Ferrite core devices", "Scott-T and Zig-Zag transformers", "Reactors, chokes, inductors, coils", "Precision inductors and chokes", "Switch-mode inductors", "DC-DC transformers", "Converter and inverter transformers"], "industries": ["Energy exploration", "Drilling operations", "Medical/biomedical", "Military", "Aerospace", "Audio", "Lighting/LEDs", "Data processing", "Industrial process control", "Communications"], "materials": ["Silicon steel", "Copper", "Aluminum", "Ferrite cores"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Single piece to OEM production volumes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house steel cutting equipment for custom core configurations", "Inventory of ~25,000 lbs high-grade silicon steel to reduce cycle time", "On-site machine shop and sheet metal department for custom bobbins, cases, and NEMA enclosures", "Engineering team with 75+ years combined design experience", "Capability from sub-miniature SMD to 1,500 lb three-phase transformers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1969 -> db, /about-us", "Headquarters Houston, Texas -> db, /about-us", "Facility 33,000 sq ft climate-controlled -> /about-us", "Employee count 51-200 -> db", "Industries served -> db, /about-us", "Capabilities (custom design, prototyping, testing, traceability, UL compliance) -> /capabilities, /services", "Products (transformers, inductors, chokes, coils, etc.) -> /capabilities, /products", "Silicon steel inventory ~25,000 lbs -> /capabilities", "Machine shop and sheet metal on-site -> /about-us, /services", "Engineering staff 75+ years combined experience -> /about-us", "High temperature up to 450\u00b0F (250\u00b0C) -> /capabilities", "High voltage up to 10kV -> /capabilities", "Single piece to OEM volumes -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Houston Transformer Company, LTD. is a leading manufacturer of custom designed transformers, inductors, chokes and related magnetic devices since 1969.", "founded_year": "1969", "employee_count": "51-200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/houston-transformer-company-ltd/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='houston-transformer-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Howard Industries is a private investment firm based in Ellisville, Mississippi, founded in 1969 by Peter Howard. Howard, who holds an economics degree from Principia College and an MBA from Columbia University, previously worked in strategic consulting at Arthur Young & Company and as a principal at another private investment firm. He established Howard Industries to provide patient capital and long-term support to management teams building market-businesses in manufacturing and specialized services.

The firm deploys its own capital across a portfolio of small and medium-sized manufacturers and business service companies, with investments ranging from $100,000 to $100 million. Since inception, Howard Industries has completed 16 investments totaling approximately $400 million, targeting companies with earnings between $1 million and $6 million or, in turnaround situations, sales exceeding $15 million. The firm operates across the U.S., Mexico, and China but prefers to partner with businesses based in the United States or the United Kingdom.

Portfolio companies span diverse sectors including motor and gear manufacturing (Jakel, Inc), specialty plastics (Continental Structural Plastics), data center infrastructure services (Critical Facilities Solutions, EDP Europe), powder coating (CPCS), fans and blowers (Comair Rotron), digital asset tracking (EnaSys), textile products (Rug Barn), bar code and RF labels (Colorflex/TTG), hinges and hardware (Lawrence Manufacturing), and consoles and racks (e-Systems Group). Howard Industries seeks niche manufacturers and service providers with defensible market positions and compelling customer value propositions.

The firm differentiates itself through its use of proprietary capital, which eliminates external fund pressures and ensures a high certainty of close. Its approach emphasizes candid communication, incremental operational improvement, and alignment with management on long-term strategy rather than short-term exits. Howard Industries remains an active director in all its investments, providing strategic guidance and operational support.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Private equity investment", "Long-term capital provision", "Strategic consulting", "Board governance", "Operational improvement support"], "industries": ["Steel processing", "Textiles", "Tubing", "Electrical components", "Motors and gears", "Specialty plastics", "Data center infrastructure", "Powder coating", "Fans and blowers", "Digital asset tracking", "Jacquard woven textiles", "Bar code and RF labels", "Hinges and hardware", "Consoles and racks", "Distribution services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Uses own capital for high certainty to close", "No pressure to sell dictated by outside partners", "Candid communication builds trust with partners", "Long-term development focus rather than quick returns", "Active board participation and operational support"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1969 -> db", "Headquartered in Ellisville, Mississippi -> db", "Principal Peter Howard founded the firm -> /", "Peter Howard education: Principia College (economics), Columbia University (MBA) -> /", "Peter Howard experience: Arthur Young & Company, private investment firm -> /", "Firm provides patient capital for long-term development -> /", "Uses own capital, $400M invested across 16 investments -> /", "Investment criteria: earnings $1-6M, sales >$15M for turnarounds -> /", "Geographic preference: US or UK based companies -> /", "Portfolio companies across multiple industries -> /", "Differentiators: own capital, no external pressure, candid communication, long-term focus -> /", "Address: 1850 Lefthand Circle, Longmont, CO 80501 -> /", "Contact:  -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Howard Industries was founded to invest in and support management teams to build market-leading businesses.", "founded_year": "1969", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='howard-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Hubco Inc. traces its roots to 1919 in Hutchinson, Kansas, when Emerson Carey and James Dick founded the Hutchinson Bag Company to produce bags for the salt industry. The business has operated continuously in Hutchinson for over a century.

Today the company functions as a textile bag manufacturer and supplier, producing custom cotton, burlap, and other fabric bags along with envelopes, cartons, and custom-printed fabrics. Its product lines include geological sample bags for mining and oil exploration, agricultural bags, cathodic protection/anode bags, retail and specialty packaging, tea towels, and food packaging. The shop offers letterpress printing on cloth bags and an online bag builder for custom orders.

Hubco serves customers in mining, oil and gas, agriculture, food packaging, retail, and specialty packaging, as well as niche markets such as leather goods (Whiskey Leatherworks), utensil makers (Origin Utensils), university soil labs (Oklahoma State University), and farms (Garber Farms).

