ET\u00ae NX6, ICHOR, HyCAP\u21224, HyPERSYNC\u2122, HyLECTRIC\u00ae -> /", "Services: Husky Advantage+Elite\u2122 monitoring, installation, training, OEM parts, audits, refurbishments, upgrades -> /", "Industries served: beverage packaging, food packaging, consumer goods, medical/pharmaceutical, electronics, automotive -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1953, Husky has led the world in plastic injection molding innovation.", "founded_year": "1953", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='husky-injection-molding-system' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1988 in Kennebunkport, Maine, Huston & Company began as a workshop dedicated to the Maine tradition of fine woodworking. The company operates from a combined showroom and workshop in Kennebunkport, where a small team of master craftsmen produces each piece by hand.

The firm designs and builds hardwood furniture for residential, corporate, academic, and library settings. Its capabilities include hand-cut dovetails, mortise-and-tenon joinery, hand-rubbed finishes, and custom shop drawings. Most work is built to order, one piece at a time, with the shop having completed hundreds of pieces ranging from bedroom sets to large conference tables and library furnishings.

Huston & Company serves architects, designers, and institutional decision-makers across the academic, library, and corporate sectors. Projects have included furnishings for small law offices and large university libraries, with the company collaborating directly with project teams to meet specific functional and aesthetic requirements.

The company’s founding mission emphasizes integrating function, form, and master-level craftsmanship into furniture that is elegant, graceful, and enduring. By focusing on wood selection, traditional joinery, and hand-applied finishes, the firm aims to deliver details not found in mass-produced alternatives.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and fabrication", "Residential furniture (dining tables, case pieces, beds, occasional tables, home office, seating, accessories)", "Institutional furnishings (conference tables, library furnishings)", "Hand-cut dovetails", "Mortise and tenon joinery", "Hand-rubbed finishes", "Shop drawings and design documentation", "Collaborative project management with architects and designers", "Custom sizing and specification"], "industries": ["Academic", "Library", "Corporate", "Residential"], "materials": ["Premium hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Custom, one-at-a-time production; hundreds of pieces completed", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-cut dovetail and mortise-and-tenon joinery on every piece", "Hand-rubbed finishes applied to premium hardwoods", "Each piece signed and dated by the maker", "Built to order, one at a time, with pricing similar to catalog pieces", "Collaborative design process with architects and designers"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 -> db", "Headquarters in Arundel, Maine -> db", "Showroom and workshop in Kennebunkport, Maine -> /about", "Designs and builds hardwood furniture for residential, corporate, academic, library -> /about", "Uses hand-cut dovetails, mortise-and-tenon joinery, hand-rubbed finishes -> /about, db", "Each piece signed and dated by maker -> /about", "Built to order, one at a time -> /about", "Serves architects, designers, institutional decision-makers -> /about", "Projects include small law offices to large university libraries -> /about", "Founding mission: integrate function, form, master-level craftsmanship -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Huston & Company designs and builds all types of hardwood furniture", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='huston-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Huston Solar operates from Lafayette, Indiana, as a division of Huston Electric Inc., a family-owned electrical contractor founded in 1939. Now in its fourth generation of Huston family ownership, the company began with electrical services and expanded into five specialized divisions—including Huston Signs, Huston Tech, Huston Generators, and Huston Solar—to serve central Indiana communities.

The solar division delivers turnkey commercial and residential solar installations and maintenance, handling every step from design and permitting to utility interconnection agreements. The company also offers $0-down financing guidance and federal tax-credit consultation.

Customers span residential homeowners, commercial property owners, industrial facilities in Indianapolis and surrounding areas, and institutions such as schools, hospitals, and warehouses across Indiana. Projects range from rooftop arrays on homes to large-scale installations for industrial complexes and educational campuses.

Huston Solar emphasizes a mission, dating to 1939, of making customers'' lives easier through turnkey solutions in electrical, technology, alternative energy, and visual communications. Core values—Safety First, Own It!, Serve Always, Lead By Example, Embrace Relationships—guide the operation. National recognition came in 2025 when the team won the Solar Games Championship at Intersolar North America, underscoring its focus on craftsmanship and innovation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar panel installation", "Commercial solar panel installation", "Industrial solar panel installation", "Institutional solar panel installation", "Solar system maintenance and service", "Turnkey solar development", "Permitting and utility interconnection management", "Energy storage system installation", "Electrical contracting", "$0-down financing facilitation", "Federal tax credit consultation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Institutional", "Educational", "Healthcare"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1939 -> db", "Headquartered in Lafayette, Indiana -> db", "Division of Huston Electric Inc. -> /", "Family-owned, fourth generation -> /about", "Five specialized divisions under Huston family -> /about", "Turnkey solar developer and installer -> /", "Handles permitting and interconnection agreements -> /about", "IBEW Local 668 electricians -> /", "24/7 live person service -> /", "Residential, commercial, industrial, institutional solar installation -> /", "Energy storage system installation -> /", "$0 down financing options -> /", "Federal tax credit consultation -> /", "2025 Solar Games Championship winner -> /", "Mission since 1939: turnkey solutions in electrical, technology, alternative energy, visual communications -> /about", "Core values: Safety First, Own It!, Serve Always, Lead By Example, Embrace Relationships -> /about", "Serves central Indiana -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Huston Solar is a division of Huston Electric Inc. that focuses on providing alternative energy solutions through commercial and residential solar panel installations and maintenance.", "founded_year": "1939", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='huston-solar-lafayette' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Hybrid Electronics is a family-owned electronic components distributor headquartered in Sanford, Florida. Founded in 2005, the company began as a Florida-based operation focused on helping manufacturers manage excess inventory and source hard-to-find parts. It has remained family-owned throughout its history.

The company operates as an independent distributor and excess-inventory buyer, offering cash purchases, consignment programs, and ongoing excess-management programs for original equipment manufacturers, electronics manufacturing services providers, and contract manufacturers. Its product range spans semiconductors, passive components, electromechanical devices, connectors, wire and cable, and board-level assemblies, with access to over 50 million part numbers from brands such as Texas Instruments, Analog Devices, and Molex. Hybrid Electronics handles transactions from single reels to full warehouse cleanouts, providing offers within one to two business days.

Customers come from commercial, industrial, medical, automotive, and high-reliability sectors, including aerospace, mil-spec, and industrial control markets. The company serves OEMs, EMS providers, and contract manufacturers that need to liquidate surplus stock or procure allocated, obsolete, or end-of-life components.

Hybrid Electronics emphasizes confidentiality, speed, and simplicity: no proprietary portals, no minimum lot sizes, and a straightforward three-step process from spreadsheet to payment. The firm positions itself as a supply-chain partner that turns idle inventory into working capital while protecting customers'' bill-of-materials data.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Excess inventory purchasing (outright and consignment)", "Electronic component distribution", "Obsolete and hard-to-find component sourcing", "Supply chain management support", "Consignment and ongoing excess programs"], "industries": ["Commercial electronics", "Industrial electronics", "Medical electronics", "Automotive electronics", "High-reliability (Hi-Rel) electronics", "Aerospace", "Military/spec (mil-spec)", "Industrial control"], "materials": ["Semiconductors (ICs, MCUs, MOSFETs, diodes, transistors)", "Passive components (capacitors, resistors, inductors)", "Electromechanical components (relays, switches, fuses)", "Connectors and interconnects", "Wire and cable assemblies", "Board-level assemblies (PCBAs, modules, backplanes)", "Industrial automation components (drives, sensors, PLC components)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "1\u20132 business days for excess inventory offers", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, Florida-based since 2005", "Cash offers or consignment on excess inventory", "Confidential handling of bill-of-materials data", "Offers within 1\u20132 business days", "No minimum lot size; simple spreadsheet-based process"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Sanford, Florida -> db", "Founded: 2005 -> /", "Ownership: Family-owned -> /", "Business model: Electronic components distributor and excess inventory buyer -> /", "Industries served: Commercial, industrial, medical, automotive, Hi-Rel -> /", "Customer types: OEMs, EMS providers, contract manufacturers -> /", "Brands carried: Texas Instruments, Analog Devices, Molex, etc. -> /", "Access to over 50 million parts -> db", "Services: Cash offers, consignment, no minimum lot, confidential, fast offers -> /", "Process: Three-step from spreadsheet to payment -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Family-owned Florida distributor \u00b7 20+ years", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum lot size", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hybrid-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Hygienic Fabrics & Filters Inc. operates from Sheboygan, Wisconsin, where it was officially founded in 1959 to supply fabricated cloth, filter socks, and tubing to Midwest cheese producers. The business traces its roots to the Sheboygan Bandage Company, which began over a century ago crafting linen cheese wraps for the region''s dairy trade.

The company provides custom converting and job-shop services from 83,000 square feet of facility space. Capabilities include steel-rule die cutting of plastic films, CNC routing, high-speed automated sheeting, slitting and rewinding up to 72 inches wide, industrial sewing, heat sealing, fabric welding, stainless steel welding, assembly, subassembly, folding, and packaging. An ISO Class 6-compliant clean room supports contaminant-sensitive work.

HFF serves food, dairy, beverage, pharmaceutical, medical device, electronics, industrial, chemical, plastics, aerospace, and defense markets. Customers include artisan cheesemakers, large consumer-products companies, defense contractors, government agencies, and disaster-relief suppliers. Products range from filtration media and filter bags to cheese bandages, dust-collection bags, transfer sleeves, and replacement filters for OEM equipment.

The firm emphasizes process development and problem-solving, drawing on over 100 years of combined staff experience in paper, film, and nonwoven converting. It offers customized equipment, quick turnaround, flexible packaging and labeling, and ISO 9001:2015-certified quality management. Core values highlight safety, short lead times, flexibility, tight internal controls, and 100% customer satisfaction.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO Class 6']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom steel rule die cutting", "CNC routing", "High-speed automated sheeting", "Industrial slitting and rewinding (up to 72\" wide)", "Industrial sewing", "Heat sealing", "Fabric welding", "Stainless steel welding", "Assembly and subassembly", "Folding", "Packaging", "ISO Class 6 clean room converting", "Custom contract industrial converting", "Contract manufacturing", "Custom manufacturing", "Process development and equipment customization", "Installation of hardware and ancillary items", "Design and construction of commercial sewing options"], "industries": ["Food and dairy", "Beverage", "Pharmaceutical", "Medical device", "Electronics", "Industrial", "Chemical", "Plastics", "Aerospace", "Defense", "Government", "Disaster relief", "Woodworking", "Food manufacturing", "Pharmaceutical manufacturing", "HVAC", "Cheese production", "Filtration"], "materials": ["Plastic films", "Polyethylene", "Polypropylene", "Polycarbonate", "PVC", "ABS", "Acrylic", "Hardwood", "Softwood", "Plywood", "Fiberboard", "Particleboard", "Foam rubber", "Neoprene", "Silicone", "Netting", "Woven fabrics", "Nonwoven materials", "Extruded films", "Paper", "Adhesive-backed materials", "Coated vinyl", "Polyester", "Webbing materials", "FDA-approved materials", "Filter media fabrics", "Cheese wrap materials"], "equipment": ["Roll slitters (up to 72\" wide)", "High-speed automated sheeting machines", "Industrial sewing machines", "Flat-bed die cutting equipment", "Stainless steel welding equipment", "CNC routing machines", "Heat sealing equipment", "Fabric welding machines", "ISO Class 6 clean room"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015-certified quality management", "ISO Class 6-compliant clean room", "83,000 sq ft facility with in-house converting, sewing, welding, and assembly", "Over 100 years of combined staff experience in web-based converting", "Willingness to customize or purchase equipment for specific projects", "Short lead times and rapid prototyping turnaround"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Sheboygan, Wisconsin -> db", "Founded: 1959 -> /about (History section)", "Facility size: 83,000 sq ft -> /about (FAQs section)", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> /services (top of page)", "ISO Class 6 clean room -> / (Clean-Room Services section) and /services", "Core capabilities: die cutting, CNC routing, sheeting, slitting, sewing, welding, assembly, packaging -> / and /services", "Industries served: food, dairy, beverage, pharmaceutical, medical, electronics, industrial, defense, government -> / and /about (History section) and /services", "Products: filtration, filter bags, cheese bandages, dust-collection bags, transfer sleeves, OEM replacement filters -> / (Products section)", "Materials: plastics, woods, rubbers, fabrics, films, nonwovens, adhesives, coated vinyl, polyester -> /services (CNC Routing and Slitting sections)", "Equipment: roll slitters up to 72\", sheeting machines, sewing machines, die cutting, welding equipment, CNC routers -> /services", "Over 100 years combined staff experience -> /about (FAQs section)", "Core values: safety, short lead times, flexibility, tight internal controls, quality, 100% customer satisfaction -> /about (Core Values section)", "Willingness to customize/purchase equipment -> /about (FAQs section)", "Company type: contract manufacturer/job shop -> / (description) and /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "HFF Converti