UPDATE companies SET description='Hypnos Medical Equipment operates from Sioux Falls, South Dakota, at 6709 S Minnesota Ave Ste. 205, where it supplies sleep therapy devices and related services. The company’s founding year and ownership details are not publicly disclosed.

The company distributes continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP) and bilevel positive airway pressure (BiPAP) devices, as well as advanced modalities such as ASV and AVAPS, from national brands including ResMed and Respironics. Services include mask fitting and selection, CPAP patient education, and troubleshooting for devices regardless of where they were purchased. No facility size, headcount, or volume figures are disclosed.

Hypnos serves the home medical equipment market, primarily patients with obstructive sleep apnea who require positive airway pressure therapy. The company works directly with patients to identify comfortable mask options and appropriate pressure settings, and it is open Monday through Friday from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.

The firm states that its exclusive focus on sleep medicine allows it to offer a wide array of treatment options, and it emphasizes its CPAP education and mask-fitting expertise as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CPAP device distribution", "BiPAP device distribution", "ASV/AVAPS device distribution", "Mask fitting and selection", "CPAP patient education", "Device troubleshooting and repair"], "industries": ["Home Medical Equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Carries all national brands including ResMed and Respironics", "Specializes exclusively in sleep medicine", "Provides CPAP education and mask fitting for each patient", "Troubleshoots devices regardless of purchase source"], "facts_used": ["Location: Sioux Falls, SD -> db", "Address: 6709 S Minnesota Ave Ste. 205, Sioux Falls, SD 57108 -> /", "Products: CPAP, BiPAP, ASV, AVAPS devices -> /", "Brands carried: ResMed, Respironics -> /", "Services: Mask fitting, CPAP education, device troubleshooting -> /", "Industry: Home Medical Equipment -> db", "Hours: Mon-Fri 8am-5pm -> /", "Contact email:  -> /", "Phone:  -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Hypnos Medical Equipment carries all national brands including Resmed & Respironics devices that can treat all severity levels of Obstructive Sleep Apnea.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hypnos-medical-equipment' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Interconnect Cable Technologies Corporation (ICTC) was founded in 1988 in Brooksville, Florida, where it maintains its corporate headquarters. The company began as a specialist in low-volume, high-mix cable and wire-harness assemblies for original equipment manufacturers worldwide.

Today ICTC operates as a full-service contract manufacturer with facilities in Brooksville and Titusville, Florida, as well as Laguna, Philippines, and Dongguan, China. Its capabilities span cable and wire harness assemblies, printed circuit board assemblies (PCBA), electronic box builds, precision machining, and turnkey assembly services. The company supports both domestic and offshore production, offering services such as custom drawing updates, first-article qualification, serialization, and a range of testing including flying probe, microsectioning, and salt fog.

ICTC serves aerospace, military and defense, industrial machinery, health care, datacom/telecom, and transportation safety sectors. Aerospace customers receive aircraft wiring and harnesses inspected to AS9102 standards; defense programs use Mil-Spec cable assemblies and power-supply system integration; medical devices are built under ISO 13485 requirements; datacom clients get molded networking and power cables; and transportation projects include video security systems for public transit and embedded data collection for roadway infrastructure.

The company emphasizes a hybrid manufacturing model that combines U.S.-based precision and intellectual-property protection with global cost efficiency. Its vertically integrated structure manages circuit card assembly, precision machining, and box build in-house, while global supply chain services provide strategic labor balancing, optimized logistics, Kanban inventory, and tariff navigation. ICTC states its mission is to simplify supply chain and manufacturing challenges and its vision is to be the most trusted, friendly, and flexible contract manufacturer.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','UL','IPC/WHMA-A-620','ITAR','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable & Wire Harness Assemblies", "PCB Assemblies (PCBA)", "Electronic Box Builds", "Precision Machining", "Turnkey Assembly Services", "Custom Drawing Updates", "First Article Qualification", "Serialization (Bar-Coding and Date Stamping)", "Testing (Flying Probe, Microsectioning, Salt Fog, Dye Pull)", "Global Supply Chain Management", "Offshore Assembly for Cost Efficiency", "Domestic Final Assembly for Compliance-Critical Builds", "Reshoring Support", "Kanban Inventory Solutions", "DFM Support", "Strategic Labor Balancing Across Regions", "Optimized Logistics and Transit Time Management", "Multi-Location Engineering Collaboration", "Reduced Lead Times Through Global Sourcing", "Tariff Navigation and Compliance Assistance"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Military & Defense", "Industrial Machinery", "Health Care", "Datacom/Telecom", "Transportation Safety"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low to high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hybrid U.S./global manufacturing model for cost efficiency and IP protection", "Vertically integrated circuit card assembly, precision machining, and box build", "Domestic final assembly for compliance-critical builds", "Kanban inventory and domestic testing solutions", "Tariff navigation and compliance assistance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 in Brooksville, Florida -> /about-us", "Headquarters Brooksville, FL; facilities in Titusville, FL; Laguna, Philippines; Dongguan, China -> /about-us", "Core services: Cable & Wire Harness, PCB Assembly, Box Build, Turnkey Assembly -> /about-us", "Certifications: AS9100D, ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, UL, IPC/WHMA-A-620, ITAR, RoHS -> /, /capabilities", "Industries served: Aerospace, Military & Defense, Industrial Machinery, Health Care, Datacom/Telecom, Transportation Safety -> /", "Capabilities: custom drawings, first article qualification, serialization, testing (flying probe, microsectioning, salt fog), precision machining, turnkey assembly -> /capabilities", "Hybrid manufacturing model: offshore assembly, domestic IP protection, strategic labor balancing, optimized logistics, multi-location engineering, domestic final assembly, reshoring support, Kanban inventory, tariff navigation -> /capabilities", "Mission: Simplify supply chain and manufacturing challenges; Vision: Most trusted, friendly, flexible contract manufacturer -> /about-us", "Leadership: Sareet Majumdar (President/CEO), Mary Alice Betts (CSO), Bill Meeler (COO), Rob Ogilbee (CFO), Shaun Majumdar (GM Asia) -> /about-us", "Volume range: Low to high volume -> /, /capabilities", "Export compliance: ITAR registered -> /, /capabilities"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "ICTC is a full-service contract manufacturer specializing in low-volume, high-mix production of cable and wire harnesses, PCB assemblies, and electronic box builds to OEM''s worldwide.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ictc-usa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='IHI Connectors, also known as International Hydraulics Inc, operates its main office, assembly, and warehouse at 7700 St. Clair Avenue in Mentor, Ohio.

The company manufactures high-tensile tin-plated aluminum electrical wire lugs, mechanical screw-type connectors, and splicing connectors for stranded and solid aluminum and copper wire in AWG, kcmil/MCM, and metric sizes. Its product line includes through-hole and surface-mount PCB terminal lugs rated from 20 to 300 amps, as well as custom OEM designs produced under blanket orders and supply contracts. The facility handles assembly, warehousing, and direct shipping, and provides STEP files for all standard stocked parts.

IHI Connectors serves the smart energy and renewable energy sectors, supplying components for EV chargers, inverter battery backup systems, server farm power supplies, solar power installations, industrial furnaces, and motion control servo power supplies.

The business emphasizes factory-direct pricing and the ability to hold blanket orders with scheduled releases. A patented Tork Krimp® ferrule system allows the use of ferrules without pre-crimping, reducing tooling, labor, and time costs. The company also offers dual multiple-wire capability for two wires per barrel in sizes from #14 AWG to #2 AWG class B/C, and interlocking lugs that can be stacked on a single bolt.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','UL Listed','UL Recognized','CSA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mechanical screw-type connector manufacturing", "Aluminum wire lug manufacturing", "Copper wire lug manufacturing", "PCB terminal lug manufacturing (through-hole and surface mount)", "Custom OEM connector design and manufacturing", "Blanket order and supply contract management", "Multiple wire per barrel capability (dual wire)", "Interlocking/stacking lug assembly", "Ferrule-compatible connector design (Tork Krimp\u00ae)", "UL/CSA listed and recognized component production", "STEP file provision for standard parts", "Warehousing and direct shipping"], "industries": ["Smart energy", "Renewable energy", "EV charging", "Inverter battery backup", "Server farm power supplies", "Solar power", "Industrial furnaces", "Motion control servo power supplies", "OEM"], "materials": ["Tin-plated aluminum", "Copper", "Aluminum", "Brass"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Factory-direct pricing on stocked lugs via LugsDirect.com", "Blanket orders and supply contracts with weekly, monthly, or quarterly releases", "Patented Tork Krimp\u00ae ferrule technology eliminates pre-crimping", "Wide range of high-current PCB terminal lugs (20A to 300A)", "Dual multiple-wire capability for 2X #14 AWG to 2X #2 AWG class B/C"], "facts_used": ["Company name: IHI Connectors (International Hydraulics Inc) -> db", "Headquarters: Mentor, Ohio -> db", "Address: 7700 St. Clair Avenue, Mentor, Ohio 44060 -> /", "Manufactures high tensile tin plated aluminum electrical wire lugs -> /", "Offers mechanical screw type connectors and splicing connectors -> /", "Produces PCB terminal lugs (through-hole and surface mount) -> /", "Provides custom OEM products and blanket orders -> /", "Serves smart energy, renewable energy, EV chargers, inverter battery backup, server farm power supplies, solar power, industrial furnaces, motion control servo power supplies -> /", "ISO 9001 certified -> db", "UL Listed and UL Recognized components -> /", "CAGE code 7RPR4 -> /", "Patented Tork Krimp\u00ae ferrule technology eliminates pre-crimping -> /", "Dual multiple wire capability for 2X #14 AWG to 2X #2 AWG class B/C -> /", "Interlocking/stacking lugs available -> /", "STEP files available for standard parts -> /", "Factory direct pricing via LugsDirect.com -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "IHI Connectors\u00ae manufactures High Tensile Tin Plated Aluminum Electrical Wire Lugs, dual rated, reusable Mechanical (screw type) and Splicing wire Connectors", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "7RPR4", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ihi-connectors-manufacturing-facility' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Impact Imports was founded in 2001 in Boise, Idaho, as a destination furniture store focused on sourcing unique artifacts from Indonesia. The company operates a warehouse showroom in Boise that is open to walk-in customers three days a week and by appointment otherwise.

The business imports and curates natural materials including live-edge wood slabs, petrified wood, river rock, andesite, onyx, and marble, which it fabricates into stone vessel sinks, pedestal sinks, boulder bathtubs, and natural stone fire pits. It also manufactures a line of rectangular gas fire tables under the IMPACT brand, built in the USA with CorTen steel and powder-coated aluminum frames. The showroom stocks reclaimed teak furniture, finished dining and coffee tables, and offers custom furniture design assistance along with on-site slab sawing, flattening, and kiln-drying services.

Impact Imports serves residential clients as well as commercial projects for lodges, eateries, cafes, and offices.

The company positions itself as a provider of refined materials that enhance visual appeal, emphasizing its direct sourcing from Indonesia and its ability to combine imported artifacts with domestic fabrication to create one-of-a-kind pieces.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Importing and sourcing from Indonesia", "Custom furniture design assistance", "Live edge wood slab processing (sawing, flattening, kiln drying)", "Stone vessel and pedestal sink fabrication", "Natural stone fire pit manufacturing", "Fire table manufacturing", "Reclaimed teak furniture fabrication"], "industries": ["Residential", "Hospitality", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Live edge wood slabs", "Petrified wood", "River rock", "Andesite", "Onyx", "Marble", "Reclaimed teak", "CorTen steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Direct sourcing of unique artifacts from Indonesia since 2001", "Warehouse showroom in Boise with walk-in and appointment access", "Custom furniture design assistance and on-site slab processing (sawing, flattening, kiln drying)", "IMPACT fire tables manufactured in the USA with CorTen steel and powder-coated aluminum", "Sustainably harvested, kiln-dried live edge wood slabs"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 -> /", "Headquartered in Boise, Idaho -> db", "Operates warehouse showroom in Boise -> /", "Sources unique artifacts from Indonesia -> /", "Offers custom furniture, live edge wood slabs, stone vessel sinks, boulder bathtubs, natural stone fire pits -> /", "Manufactures IMPACT fire tables in USA -> /", "Sells reclaimed teak furniture -> /", "Provides slab sawing, flattening, kiln drying -> /", "Serves homes, lodges, eateries, cafes, offices -> /", "Positions as provider of refined materials to enhance visual appeal -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Impact Imports is a unique Boise, Idaho destination furniture store", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='impact-imports' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='IMS Woodworking Inc. operates from Arlington, Massachusetts, where it was founded in 2011. The company provides carpentry and woodworking services to residential and commercial clients throughout the area.

The shop focuses on custom interior woodwork, including kitchen finishes, custom cabinets, planned furniture, stairs and handrails, walk-in closets, and addition services such as door, window, and trim installation. The company reports having completed over 100 projects since its inception, with a stated track record of 10 to 15 years in the trade.

Customers range from homeowners seeking custom cabinetry and built-in furniture to commercial clients needing finish carpentry for office or retail spaces.

IMS Woodworking emphasizes personalized design solutions, modern aesthetics, and a balance of quality materials with competitive pricing. The company positions its ability to deliver custom pieces quickly as a core part of its service model, highlighting modern design, high-quality materials, and safety as guiding principles.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinet making", "Furniture making", "Stair and handrail fabrication", "Finish carpentry", "Trim installation", "Door and window installation", "Kitchen finishing", "Walk-in closet systems"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Interior remodeling"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Personalized design solutions for each customer", "Custom furniture and cabinets delivered quickly", "Competitive pricing without compromising material quality", "Modern design, high-quality materials, and safety focus"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Arlington, MA -> db", "Founded: 2011 -> db", "Services: kitchen finishes, custom cabinets, planned furniture, stairs & handrails, walk-in closets, addition services (doors, windows, trim) -> /", "Residential and commercial customers -> /", "Over 100 completed projects -> /", "10-15 years experience claimed -> /", "Personalized solutions, modern design, quality materials, competitive pricing -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Beautiful, modern and efficient cabinets. Our carpenters offer the best services to ensure authentic pieces at the best price for your home or office.", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ims-woodworking-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ITW Food Equipment Group is headquartered in Troy, Ohio. The group traces its roots to 1830 with the founding of Bonnet in Europe and brings together brands such as Hobart (120 years), Vulcan (150 years), Baxter (50-plus years), Traulsen, Foster, Wolf, and Stero. The company operates as a family of premium brands dedicated to commercial food equipment.

The group designs, manufactures, and services a broad range of commercial food equipment including cooking, refrigeration, warewashing, and bakery systems. Its brands collectively offer nearly 600 ENERGY STAR certified products. Hobart maintains nearly 200 offices and 1,500 factory-trained service technicians, covering 95% of service customers within 50 miles. Innovation is central: more than 1,000 staff members hold at least one invention, and in 2013 over 70% of ITW patent applications were commercialized. Key technologies include the Advansys energy recovery system for dishwashers, finless condenser coils in refrigeration, infrared cooking in charbroilers and griddles, and the SmartConnect365 remote monitoring platform.

ITW Food Equipment serves the foodservice, food retail, bakery, restaurant, hotel, school, rest-home catering, and broader catering equipment markets worldwide. Customers range from independent restaurants to large institutional kitchens and food retail operations.

The company emphasizes customer-driven innovation, sustainable leadership, and local service depth. It has earned the EPA ENERGY STAR Partner of the Year award every year since 2008, receiving the Sustained Excellence Award in 2024. Foster attained the Carbon Trust Standard for carbon reduction. The group’s differentiation rests on its extensive service network, high rate of patent commercialization, and energy- and water-saving equipment technologies.', certifications=ARRAY['ENERGY STAR','Carbon Trust Standard']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial cooking equipment manufacturing", "Commercial refrigeration manufacturing", "Warewashing equipment manufacturing", "Bakery equipment manufacturing", "Equipment installation", "Equipment maintenance and service", "Energy recovery systems (Advansys)", "Remote equipment monitoring (SmartConnect365)", "Finless condenser coil technology", "Deliming systems for commercial dishwashers", "Infrared cooking technology", "Carbon footprint reduction consulting"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Food retail", "Bakery", "Restaurant", "Hotel", "School", "Rest-home catering", "Catering equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Advansys (Hobart Energy Recovery System)", "Foster EcoPro Cabinets", "Traulsen solid-door R&A and G-Series models", "Vulcan PowerFry5 with FivePass heat transfer system", "Bonnet Precisio Oven with Full Cleaning System", "SmartConnect365 suite of apps", "Rotating rack oven (ENERGY STAR certified)", "Charbroilers and griddles with infrared technology"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nearly 600 ENERGY STAR certified products across all brands", "Hobart service network within 50 miles of 95% of customers", "Over 1,000 staff members with at least one invention", "Advansys energy recovery system cuts energy costs up to 50% and water use up to 90%", "SmartConnect365 remote monitoring suite for kitchen equipment"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Troy, Ohio -> db", "Founded 1830