UPDATE companies SET description='Icon Modern was founded in 2007 by Rocky Levy and Aaron Tvrdy in Chicago, Illinois. The founders, who met through a shared passion for sustainable design, started in a garage and quickly secured projects with national brands such as Starbucks, Whole Foods, and Twitter.

The company produces commercial furniture and architectural elements — conference tables, community tables, reception desks, space dividers, ceiling elements, feature walls, planters, and countertops — using a broad range of materials including urban hardwoods, steel, stone, glass, and veneers. Icon Modern imposes no minimum or maximum order quantities and emphasizes shorter lead times through a streamlined process.

The firm serves architects, interior designers, and corporate clients across hospitality, retail, technology, and corporate office sectors. Notable projects include installations for Caterpillar, Jump Trading, and IPG, alongside the earlier brand-name work. A dedicated project manager oversees each job from concept through installation, handling engineering, detailing, and logistics on the client''s behalf.

Icon Modern''s founding mission centers on sustainability and creative reuse: sourcing all materials within a 100-mile radius of its Chicago shop and giving urban trees a second life as furniture. The team, which includes architects and designers, aims to make custom fabrication more accessible to designers by offering a wider material palette and a collaborative, end-to-end service that eliminates the need for clients to coordinate multiple vendors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture fabrication", "Architectural element fabrication", "CNC machining", "Metal fabrication and welding", "Woodworking (urban wood, veneers, solid wood)", "Powder coating (custom colors, matte, semi-gloss, brass patina)", "Stone fabrication (quartz)", "Glass fabrication", "3D rendering and shop drawings", "Engineering and value engineering", "Prototyping", "Project management", "Installation oversight"], "industries": ["Commercial furniture", "Architectural elements", "Interior design", "Hospitality", "Retail", "Technology", "Corporate offices"], "materials": ["Urban hardwoods (elm, maple, walnut, spalted maple)", "Steel (hot rolled, tube, sheet)", "Stone (quartz)", "Glass", "Wood veneers (oak, walnut)", "Sintra (PVC foam board)", "Preserved moss", "Wire mesh", "Expanded metal", "Corrugated metal", "Cast iron", "Antique mirror", "Powder coat finishes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum or maximum order quantities", "In-house project management from concept through installation", "Materials sourced within 100-mile radius of Chicago shop", "Team includes architects and designers who understand designer needs", "Shorter lead times through streamlined process"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2007 by Rocky Levy and Aaron Tvrdy -> /about-us", "Started in garage, now 10,000 sq ft West Loop showroom -> /about-us", "Sources materials within 100-mile radius -> /about-us", "Projects with Starbucks, Whole Foods, Twitter -> /about-us", "15+ years in custom fabrication -> /", "No minimums or maximums -> /", "Shorter lead times -> /", "Services: dedicated project manager, engineering+VE, shop drawings, 3D renderings, prototyping -> /", "Team includes architects and designers -> /", "Products: conference tables, community tables, reception desks, space dividers, ceiling elements, feature walls, planters, countertops -> /", "Materials: urban wood, steel, stone, glass, veneers, sintra, moss, wire mesh, expanded metal, corrugated metal, cast iron, antique mirror, powder coat -> /, /about-us", "Industries: hospitality (Starbucks), retail (Whole Foods), tech (Twitter), corporate (Caterpillar, Jump Trading, IPG) -> /about-us, /", "Sustainability mission: creative reuse of urban trees -> /about-us", "Headquarters: Chicago, Illinois -> db, /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "full-service custom fabrication company specializing in commercial furniture and architectural elements", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimums or maximums", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='icon-modern' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Icon Solar was founded in 2009 in Milford, Ohio, and has grown into a regional solar installation company serving Ohio, Kentucky, and Indiana. The company operates as a locally owned installer without outside subcontractors, handling every project directly from design through grid connection.

The firm provides turnkey residential and commercial solar installations, including system design, permitting, panel mounting, inverter and battery storage integration, and utility interconnection. It partners with manufacturers such as Franklin WH Home Battery, Enphase Ensemble, and Tesla Powerwall to supply equipment, and emphasizes premium components like black-on-black solar panels and module-level power electronics. Icon Solar describes itself as one of the largest residential installers in the tri-state area, though it does not disclose facility size or headcount.

The company also works with municipal solar programs and the ''Find It Duke'' referral network. Projects range from rooftop arrays for single-family homes to commercial systems aimed at reducing overhead energy costs.

Icon Solar differentiates itself by refusing to subcontract work, maintaining direct manufacturer relationships, and offering 25-year production warranties on both panels and inverters. It cites an A+ Better Business Bureau rating with zero complaints, a 4.8 Google review score, and a typical installation timeline of about six weeks from permit to grid connection as evidence of its reliability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar panel installation", "Turnkey system design and permitting", "Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Battery storage integration (Franklin WH, Enphase Ensemble, Tesla Powerwall)", "Module-level power electronics (MLPE) inverter installation", "Grid interconnection coordination", "Solar financing consultation"], "industries": ["Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Renewable energy services", "Energy storage installation"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Franklin WH Home Battery", "Enphase Ensemble", "Tesla Powerwall", "MLPE inverter systems", "Black-on-black solar panels"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Approximately 6 weeks from permit to grid connection", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No subcontractors; all installation performed by in-house teams", "Direct partnerships with Franklin WH Home Battery, Enphase Ensemble, and Tesla Powerwall", "Turnkey service covering design, permitting, installation, and grid interconnection", "25-year production warranties on panels and inverters", "BBB A+ rating with zero complaints"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 -> db", "Headquarters Milford, Ohio -> db", "Serves Ohio, Kentucky, Indiana -> page /", "No subcontractors used -> page /", "Partners with Franklin WH Home Battery, Enphase Ensemble, Tesla Powerwall -> page /", "Turnkey installation service -> page /", "25-year production warranties on panels and inverters -> page /about-us", "BBB A+ rating with zero complaints -> page /about-us", "Google 4.8 rating -> page